                                <comments>
                            <comment id="16949971" author="ignitetcbot" created="Sat, 12 Oct 2019 09:12:44 +0000"  >&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; style=&quot;border-color: #ccc;border-style: dashed;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;panelHeader&quot; style=&quot;border-bottom-width: 1px;border-bottom-style: dashed;border-bottom-color: #ccc;background-color: #D6F7C1;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Branch: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;pull/6965/head&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; Base: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;master&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; : No blockers found!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=4686231&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_RunAll&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;TeamCity &lt;b&gt;--&amp;gt; Run :: All&lt;/b&gt; Results&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16950874" author="zzzadruga" created="Mon, 14 Oct 2019 10:03:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=avinogradov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;avinogradov&quot;&gt;avinogradov&lt;/a&gt;, please, review my change.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16951642" author="avinogradov" created="Tue, 15 Oct 2019 06:17:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zzzadruga&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zzzadruga&quot;&gt;zzzadruga&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Is there any reason to keep oomeHnd (to check only OutOfMemoryError) at other threadpools?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16951844" author="zzzadruga" created="Tue, 15 Oct 2019 11:24:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=avinogradov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;avinogradov&quot;&gt;avinogradov&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I believe that other thread pools are not critical, it is worth handling exceptions the only if it is OOM. Rebalance is a critical operation, and all exceptions must be handled by failure handler.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16951880" author="avinogradov" created="Tue, 15 Oct 2019 12:07:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zzzadruga&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zzzadruga&quot;&gt;zzzadruga&lt;/a&gt;,&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some other pools seems to be even more critical that rebalance pool.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;could you provide some tips as an author of&#160;oomeHnd?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16952552" author="alex_pl" created="Wed, 16 Oct 2019 06:48:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=avinogradov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;avinogradov&quot;&gt;avinogradov&lt;/a&gt;&#160;OOME should be handled by failure handler in any pool, since if OOME fired once it may happen again at any time in some other unpredictable place and we can&apos;t be sure about node consistency in this case. General-purpose pools should not handle all errors and unpredicted thread terminations.&#160;Errors which proposed to top-level should be handled only for critical workers on workers&apos; level. There is usually catch or finally block with failure handler call for such workers.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16952567" author="avinogradov" created="Wed, 16 Oct 2019 07:10:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt;,&#160;It looks like better case is to handle errors properly on workers&apos; level, but also extend oomeHnd to handle any unhandled errors?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also, we may add an assertion that only OOME is suitable at&#160;oomeHnd?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16952575" author="alex_pl" created="Wed, 16 Oct 2019 07:26:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=avinogradov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;avinogradov&quot;&gt;avinogradov&lt;/a&gt;, I do not fully understand your proposal. Why should we extend oomeHnd to handle any other errors? Why should we add an assertion? oomeHnd should only handle OOME and pass all other errors untouched (some of them can be expected, it depends on a worker).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16952591" author="avinogradov" created="Wed, 16 Oct 2019 08:00:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt;, just a&#160;foolproof proposal &lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/emoticons/wink.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ok, let&apos;s keep semantic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zzzadruga&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zzzadruga&quot;&gt;zzzadruga&lt;/a&gt;, seems we just have to provide proper catch instead of handlers improvements.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17094272" author="ignitetcbot" created="Tue, 28 Apr 2020 08:04:59 +0000"  >&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; style=&quot;border-color: #ccc;border-style: dashed;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;panelHeader&quot; style=&quot;border-bottom-width: 1px;border-bottom-style: dashed;border-bottom-color: #ccc;background-color: #D6F7C1;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Branch: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;pull/6965/head&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; Base: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;master&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; : No blockers found!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=5266787&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_RunAll&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;TeamCity &lt;b&gt;--&amp;gt; Run :: All&lt;/b&gt; Results&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17095261" author="avinogradov" created="Wed, 29 Apr 2020 09:05:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zzzadruga&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zzzadruga&quot;&gt;zzzadruga&lt;/a&gt;,&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LGTM.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AFAICS, 2.8.1 is also the aim?&lt;br/&gt;
Could you please provide PR to 2.8.1 too?&lt;br/&gt;
I&apos;ll merge both and resolve the issue.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17095566" author="zzzadruga" created="Wed, 29 Apr 2020 15:48:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=avinogradov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;avinogradov&quot;&gt;avinogradov&lt;/a&gt;, thanks for the review. I created &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/7761&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;new PR&lt;/a&gt; for Ignite 2.8.1. &lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17096461" author="ignitetcbot" created="Thu, 30 Apr 2020 11:57:45 +0000"  >&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; style=&quot;border-color: #ccc;border-style: dashed;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;panelHeader&quot; style=&quot;border-bottom-width: 1px;border-bottom-style: dashed;border-bottom-color: #ccc;background-color: #D6F7C1;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Branch: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;pull/6965/head&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; Base: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;master&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; : No blockers found!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
